<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan buys 80,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys 80,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taiwan Flour Mills Association on Thursday bought two shipments totalling 80,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, with components coming from both Cargill and Marubeni, traders said.  </p>
<p>Each shipment contains Dark Northern Spring (DNS), Hard Red Winter (HRW) and White Wheat (WW) and both were slated for delivery from the Pacific Northwest, traders said.</p>
<p>Traders said both shipments were No.1 grade wheat.</p>
<p>Members of the wheat association include President Enterprise, Tai Yu Products, Chia Hsin, Formosa Oilseed, Lien Hwa Industry and other wheat millers.  </p>
<p>Details of the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Supplier   Type  Tonnes  Delivery Date  Price     Freight</p>
<p>		 One	    Nov 20-Dec 10		$19.00</p>
<p>  Cargill    DNS  24,500		     $210.64</p>
<p>  Marubeni   HRW  11,000		     $199.93</p>
<p>  Cargill     WW   4,500		     $163.64</p>
<p>		 Two	    Nov 30-Dec 20		$19.00</p>
<p>  Marubeni   DNS  23,100		     $204.24</p>
<p>  Marubeni   HRW  10,200		     $199.23</p>
<p>  Cargill     WW   6,700		     $162.96</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
